#reason src/main/lantern-host-avatar.ts Turns host avatar URLs into capped data URIs in the main process, since the renderer's CSP cannot load remote images
#reason src/renderer/assets/icons/pen.svg Icon for the reasons row in the local comparison's Context section
#reason src/renderer/pr-info/index.ts Builds the PR hover card and the sidebar byline and footer from one place so both stay in sync
#reason test/lantern-host-avatar.test.ts Covers avatar fetching: size cap, image types, redirects and the failure cache
#reason test/lantern-host-info.test.ts Covers reading PR details from Bitbucket and GitHub replies, keeping only well-formed fields
#reason test/pr-info.test.ts Covers the PR card and sidebar byline: dates, avatars, approvals, escaping and the local card
#reason docs/primitives.md Documents setTipCard for rich tooltip cards and the new timeAgo and exactTime date helpers so other features reuse them
#reason src/main/lantern-host-github.ts Reads author, dates, comment count, draft flag and requested reviewers from the GitHub reply so GitHub PRs get the same hover card as Bitbucket ones
#reason src/main/lantern-host-request.ts Reads author, dates, comment counts and reviewer verdicts from the Bitbucket reply, and shares its field readers with the GitHub request
#reason src/main/lantern-host-status.ts Carries the host's PR info with avatars into the PR list and refreshes it when reviews or the update time change
#reason src/main/lantern-prs.ts Gives PRs without host data an author and last update from git, so every card can still say who opened it
#reason src/main/lantern-types.ts Adds the PR info shape (author, dates, reviewers, draft) shared by the host and git sources and the renderer
#reason src/renderer/features/lantern.ts Reports a failed reasons run in the bottom-bar problems log instead of inside the sidebar
#reason src/renderer/floating.css Gives the PR hover card a fixed width so its rows line up
#reason src/renderer/lantern-problems/index.ts Uses the shared plural helper instead of its own copy
#reason src/renderer/lantern-prs.css Styles the PR card, the one-card sidebar header with its action bar, and the Context section for local comparisons
#reason src/renderer/lantern.css Gives the PR hover card the Lantern colour tokens, since the tooltip renders outside the Lantern panel
#reason src/renderer/lib/comparemodal.ts Uses the shared plural helper instead of its own copy
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternmacro.ts Uses the shared plural helper instead of its own copy
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternprdescribe.ts Puts the Show details toggle in the header's action bar so it sits with the other PR actions
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternprpanel.ts Rebuilds the sidebar PR header as one card with an action bar, and gives local comparisons a Context section for reasons and mapping
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternprs.ts Shows the PR card on hovering a PR tab and drops the tooltip from the close buttons
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternview.ts Stops passing the reasons note to the panel now that errors go to the problems log
#reason src/renderer/lib/util.ts Shares plural, timeAgo and exactTime so PR dates and counts read the same everywhere
#reason src/renderer/theme.css Adds a stronger border and a secondary button colour that keep the navy hue of the top bar
#reason src/renderer/tooltip/index.ts Lets a tooltip show a rich card built when it opens, for the PR hover card
#reason test/lantern-host-status.test.ts Covers merging host PR info into the list and refreshing when reviews change
#reason test/lantern-pr-describe-card.test.ts Follows the description moving into the card's story section
#reason test/lantern-pr-panel.test.ts Follows the byline replacing the old people row in the sidebar header
#reason test/lantern-pr-refresh.test.ts Checks the Context section's Write reasons button and that a failure lands in the problems log
#reason test/lantern-pr-visibility.test.ts Follows the close button losing its tooltip
#reason test/tooltip.test.ts Covers tooltips that show a rich card
#story Hovering a pull request shows who, when and where review stands
